  "worked_solution": "First, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t) \\\\  & =2t\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t-{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ the velocity is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed is $|-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}|=\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}\u22482.47\\,\\text{m/s}$ to 2 decimal places.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
